{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Seir.</b> We do not know his genealogy, and Scripture mentions them to separate the genealogies of Seir and Esau, because Israel will be commanded regarding the children of Esau." "The Horite, like Hurai of Judah (Jeremiah 27:20 [27:20 in KJV]). Its meaning is greatness, and it may be from the root of ואורנים חורי (Isaiah 19:9 [sic]), which is whiteness, and so the Targum said, and the nobles were likened to whiteness because there is nothing like it before the eyes, and it is like light, and the opposite of this is בל יתיצב לפני חשוכים (Proverbs 22:29 [sic]):"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {1 "The verse citation ישעיה י\"ט ט' (Isaiah 19:9) is given as printed; Ibn Ezra likely refers to a different verse. משלי כ\"ב כ\"ט also does not match the quoted phrase precisely; citations preserved as in source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:09.538223210Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}